# Luggage: make the service and gate side actionable.
add('guides/luggage-before-flight-japan','Luggage Storage Before a Flight in Japan: Avoid Backtracking',
 'Choose hotel, station or airport storage by your return route, compare Tokyo and Osaka counter examples and distinguish storage from delivery before a flight.',
 'The best storage point is not necessarily the nearest locker. It is the place you can return to once, collect before closing and leave from toward the airport. Gate side and collection time matter as much as the daily fee.',[
 sec('storage-choice','Choose the service around the journey',table(['Option','Works well when…','Weak point'],[
 ('Hotel storage','The hotel is still on the airport route and collection is confirmed','A free bag service can cost a large cross-city return journey.'),('Station locker','The compartment fits, is available and is on the correct side of the gates','A suitcase may not fit; the quoted fee for a small locker may be irrelevant.'),('Staffed station counter','You want a named collection point with published service hours','You must return while that specific service is available, not merely while the station is open.'),('Airport storage','You are already at the airport and staying nearby','Returning to the city creates another outward and return journey.'),('Delivery','The delivery date and airport collection window are confirmed for your flight','It is not instant storage. A missed cutoff or wrong pickup terminal defeats the plan.')])) ,
 sec('storage-examples','Concrete station choices and the decisions they change',table(['Place','Published option','How to use the information'],[
 ('Tokyo Station','GRANSTA B1 inside JR gates, 08:30–21:00 with a separate “until 20:30” same-day note; 1F JR EAST Travel Service Center outside gates, 08:30–20:00. Listed S/M/L ¥500/¥1,000/¥2,000.','Choose gate access you actually have; collect before the service cutoff. These terms are from the operator’s 23 May 2025 listing.'),('Namba','n・e・s・t: ¥800/item/day, 09:00–21:00; tourism listing dated 1 October 2025, with size/weight limits.','Fits a Namba visit and Nankai return, subject to acceptance and current conditions.'),('Osaka Station','Crosta Osaka: outside gates, north-central 1F, ¥1,000/day, 09:00–20:00 on the operator’s page.','Fits an Umeda stop. Save the named counter location rather than a general Osaka Station pin.')])+p('The fee for a specific counter does not apply to every nearby locker. We have not verified live capacity or the exact fee of every compartment. For unusual sizes, use the provider’s acceptance rules before leaving the bag.')),
 sec('storage-difference','A cheap hotel pickup can make the day more expensive in time',p('Suppose you finish in Ginza but leave the bag in Shinjuku. The journey is Ginza → hotel → departure station → airport, not Ginza → airport. The return walk, reception queue and repacking belong before the airport train. Compare that complete loop with paid storage on the departure corridor.')+p('If the bag is already at Shinagawa and the flight is from Haneda, a nearby meal can eliminate the second city journey. If it is at Keisei-Ueno and the flight is from Narita, keeping the final stop around Ueno avoids returning west. The right choice is often a smaller sightseeing area.')),
 sec('storage-collection','Before walking away, save the details you will need to return',ul(['The counter or locker bank’s name, floor, gate side and an identifying photo or map pin.','The receipt, locker number and access method, kept outside the stored bag.','The collection deadline, including any special same-day rule.','Enough time to retrieve and repack purchases before the train. The retrieval allowance is separate from the walk back.'])+p('Keep passports, medication and required travel documents with you. If storage is full, choose a bag-friendly meal and shorten the visit; searching several stations can cost the afternoon.')),
 sec('airport-storage','At the airport: collect before entering the wrong side',p('Haneda lists its coin lockers outside the departure gates, with terminal-specific conditions. Collect those bags before leaving the public area. Narita lists storage providers by terminal rather than one universal fee; choose the counter in the terminal you can actually reach at collection time.')+p('The planner can include a return to the storage area you enter, but it does not know your exact hotel room, locker position or reception queue. Use the area-level allowance as a model and allow extra time for the actual collection point.'))
 ],['gransta','namba-bags','crosta','hnd-locker','nrt-storage'],'HND',[('/after-hotel-checkout-tokyo/','Tokyo checkout: match the last stop to the bag location'),('/guides/after-hotel-checkout-osaka/','Osaka checkout: Namba and Umeda choices'),('/how-early-arrive-haneda-airport/','Haneda leave-by examples')])
add('guides/haneda-terminal-3-departure-guide','Haneda Terminal 3 Departures: Floors, Map & What to Do',
 'Find T3’s departure floor, public-side food and observation deck, then handle luggage, lounge access and the walk from the airport station without losing procedure time.',
 'At Haneda Terminal 3, go to <strong>3F for international departures</strong>. Find your flight’s current check-in counter before choosing food or shopping. The public-side Edo Ko-ji and observation deck are different from shops and lounges beyond security.',[
 sec('t3-floors','A floor guide that follows your departure',table(['Place','What it is useful for','Access boundary'],[
 ('3F departure lobby','Flight displays, airline check-in and the route into security','Public side until departure procedures.'),('4F Edo Ko-ji','A meal or a brief souvenir browse before procedures, when time allows','Public side. You cannot treat it as a meal beside your boarding gate.'),('5F observation deck','A short aircraft view','Public side; weather restrictions can close it.'),('International departure area','Gate, duty-free shopping and eligible lounges','After security and departure immigration. Find the gate and deadline before settling down.')])+p(a(S['hnd-map'][0],'Open the official T3 floor guide')+' and use its floor labels rather than a broad airport map pin. If your booking uses T2, this is not the departure lobby for your flight.')),
 sec('t3-station','From the station, follow Departures—not Arrivals','<ol><li>Get off at <strong>Haneda Airport Terminal 3</strong>, not the T1/T2 rail stop.</li><li>Use the signed route to <strong>Departures / 3F</strong>. With a case or stroller, follow lifts rather than improvising through another floor.</li><li>Read your flight number on the display and locate the counter. Assignments can change by flight and day.</li><li>Complete the airline’s baggage and document requirements, then security and departure immigration.</li><li>Find the boarding gate and its deadline before deciding how long to spend in a shop or lounge.</li></ol>'+p('For a planning example, reserve 20 minutes for the station-to-counter movement when calculating the city journey. That is our rounded allowance for orientation and lifts, not a measured promise from every platform to every counter. '+a(S['keikyu-floor'][0],'Keikyu’s station-to-terminal drawings')+' show the rail approach.')),
 sec('t3-extra','Choose the extra stop around the next required procedure',table(['Genuinely spare time','A suitable use'],[
 ('15–20 minutes','Stay near the required procedure for a toilet stop, water or a nearby quick purchase.'),('30–45 minutes','If still public-side, take a short deck visit or browse, with walking back included.'),('Around an hour or more','A seated meal can work if the queue, service and next procedure leave room. Ask about a wait before joining it.')])+p('These are optional-visit allowances, not permission to arrive 15, 30 or 60 minutes before takeoff. Once airside, choose facilities near the actual gate route; do not plan to return to Edo Ko-ji for dinner.')),
 sec('t3-bags-lounge','Two services that are easy to misunderstand',p('<strong>Locker storage:</strong> Haneda lists coin lockers outside the gates. Save the locker position and collect the bag before departure procedures. An empty small compartment does not establish that your large case can be stored.')+p('<strong>TIAT LOUNGE:</strong> this is not an unrestricted public waiting room. Access depends on the lounge’s location, your flight and the accepted airline/card or paid-entry conditions. A card accepted at a domestic POWER LOUNGE is not automatically accepted at TIAT. Use the current official lounge listing before relying on admission; capacity and hours do not guarantee a seat.')),
 sec('t3-before-counter','If you arrive before your counter opens',p('Keep the case and essentials on the public side, find an open nearby meal or rest option and return for the airline’s opening time. An open terminal does not mean every counter or restaurant is operating. For a wait through the night, T3’s overnight eligibility rules matter as well as opening hours.')+p(a('/guides/haneda-airport-open-24-hours/','Read the overnight rules and early-flight options')+'.'))
 ],['hnd-dep','hnd-map','keikyu-floor','hnd-locker','hnd-lounge','hnd-deck'],'HND',[('/how-early-arrive-haneda-airport/','How early to reach the correct Haneda terminal'),('/places/haneda-airport/','Choose one airport meal or view'),('/guides/luggage-before-flight-japan/','Storage and collection before a flight')])
add('guides/haneda-airport-open-24-hours','Is Haneda Airport Open 24 Hours? Overnight & Early Flights',
 'Understand T3 overnight eligibility, T1/T2 hours, counter and restaurant limits, and the date and transport plan needed for an early or after-midnight Haneda flight.',
 '<strong>Haneda Terminal 3 is generally open 24 hours</strong>, but that rule does not apply to every terminal or service. The airport says T3 overnight stays are for people who have used or will use international flights. A domestic-only early departure is not a reason to assume T3 is available as accommodation.',[
 sec('overnight-hours','The building can be open while your service is closed',table(['Area or service','What to plan around'],[
 ('T3 building','Generally 24 hours, with international-flight eligibility for overnight stays under airport rules.'),('T1 / T2 domestic areas','Generally 05:00–24:00, with lobby operation tied to last flights. Overnight lobby stays after closure are generally unavailable.'),('T2 international departures','Opens at 05:00; the departure lobby remains open until after the last departure. Do not borrow T3’s 24-hour rule.'),('Airline counter / bag drop / security','Operation follows the relevant airline, flight and checkpoint. The building’s opening time is not your counter’s opening time.'),('Food, shops and transport','Each has its own schedule. A 24-hour terminal does not imply all-night restaurants or continuous trains.')])) ,
 sec('overnight-rest','Choose between an eligible wait and a bookable bed',p('An eligible public-side overnight wait in T3 provides no reserved bed, quiet space or guaranteed charging seat. Keep flight details and documents accessible and follow staff directions. For travelers with children, a long flight ahead or a need for reliable sleep, a bookable room can be a better use of the night.')+p('The airport hotel directory lists The Royal Park Hotel Tokyo Haneda at T3, Haneda Excel Hotel Tokyu at T2 and First Cabin Haneda Terminal 1. Choose using the actual route to your departure terminal at the time you need it. Do not assume an “airport hotel” has a shuttle running early enough, and do not confuse public-side hotel rooms with transit-only facilities. '+a(S['hnd-hotel'][0],'See the airport’s hotel locations and provider links')+'.')),
 sec('midnight','A 00:30 flight is on the ticket’s next date',p('<strong>Flight: 21 November, 00:30. Three-hour terminal-ready target: 20 November, 21:30.</strong> Travel on the evening of 20 November. Arriving on the evening of 21 November would be a day late for this flight.')+p('If the complete journey takes 90 minutes and bag collection 20 minutes in your selected example, begin collection at <strong>19:40 on 20 November</strong>. Enter the ticket’s flight date in the planner and the previous date for your free time. It uses Japan Standard Time (JST).')),
 sec('first-train','For a 06:30 flight, the first train may not solve the journey',p('Under this site’s three-hour policy, a 06:30 departure gives a 03:30 target. Compare the airline’s actual instructions with transport operating hours before choosing where to spend the night. If a suitable train does not run, the options are an eligible T3 overnight wait, accommodation with a workable access plan, or a prearranged road transfer.')+p('Keikyu publishes late-night/early-morning access guidance from its airport-access page. Use an actual dated route for the chosen terminal. A road transfer also needs a real pickup location, availability and a budget; it should not be an unplanned assumption after missing the last train.')),
 sec('overnight-food','Make the overnight wait easier before leaving the city',ul(['Eat before travel if your preferred terminal restaurant will be closed. Keep a drink or simple food plan that respects facility rules.','Keep baby supplies, medication, documents and a charger outside the case until bag drop really opens.','Use storage only if you can reach and retrieve from that exact service during its operating hours.','For a short break, T3’s deck is listed as open 24 hours, subject to weather closure. It is not a sleeping facility.'])+earlier())
 ],['hnd-hours','hnd-hotel','keikyu','hnd-deck'],'HND',[('/guides/haneda-terminal-3-departure-guide/','T3 departure floors and public-side facilities'),('/how-early-arrive-haneda-airport/','Haneda arrival and luggage-pickup calculations')])
